The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font vs. a music font."}]}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}]},{"name":"usesPlusMinus","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether plus and minus symbols should be used instead of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" if not specified."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesplusminus:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"MXLDegree.Alter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPosition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"usesPlusMinus","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Initializer","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLDegreeV5AlterV5value8position4font5color13usesPlusMinusAESd_AA11MXLPositionVAA7MXLFontVAA8MXLColorVSgSbSgtcfc","title":"init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","symbolKind":"init","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct/init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"value","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","text":"MXLPosition","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"usesPlusMinus","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","title":"init(value:position:font:color:usesPlusMinus:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"code":"MXLDegree.Alter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct\/init(value:position:font:color:usesplusminus:)"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree/Alter-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Alter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree\/Alter-swift.struct","title":"MXLDegree.Alter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree-alter type represents the chromatic alteration for the current degree. If the degree-type value is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alter or subtract, the degree-alter value is relative to the degree already in the chord based on its kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element. If the degree-type value is add, the degree-alter is relative to a dominant chord (major and perfect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intervals except for a minor seventh). The plus-minus attribute is used to indicate if plus and minus symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be used instead of sharp and flat symbols to display the degree alteration. It is no if not specified."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Alter","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree\/alter-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"title":"MXLPosition"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDegree":{"title":"MXLDegree","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLDegree"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The degree type is used to add, alter, or subtract individual notes in the chord. The print-object attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used to keep the degree from printing separately when it has already taken into account in the text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute of the kind element. The degree-value and degree-type text attributes specify how the value and type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the degree should be displayed."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDegree","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDegree","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldegree"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"}}}